    "answer": "to: {break/be-smashed} | {split/crack/fissure/be-torn} | {be-divided-(opinion,-vote,-etc.)/split-(e.g.-of-a-party)} | {come-to-light/become-clear/be-identified/be-revealed} | be-distorted-(of-a-sound) | be-divisible-(without-a-remainder) | go-below-a-minimum",
    "mnemonic": "Remember how <ja>割る</ja> is \"to divide\"? Now you're learning the intransitive version. Instead of you doing the dividing, something just gets divided or split up. So this is <vocabulary>to be divided</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>to be split</vocabulary>.\n\nIt can also mean <vocabulary>to break</vocabulary>, as in <ja>ワイングラスが割れる</ja> (the wine glass breaks). After all, when an object breaks, it’s divided into parts, right?",
    "readingMnemonic": "The reading is shared with <ja>割る</ja>."
